    """Remove dead and trivial phi nodes to a fixpoint.

    A phi is dead when its result has no user outside the set of phis
    (phi-only cycles -- e.g. a loop-carried temporary nobody reads --
    therefore evaporate as a whole).  A phi is trivial when all of its
    incoming values are the same, ignoring its own result and chasing
    replacements through previously removed phis.  The two rules are
    repeated together until neither applies.
    """
    while True:
        removed = self._remove_dead_phis(blocks)
        removed |= self._remove_trivial_phis(blocks)
        if not removed:
            return

